  },
  {
    "episode_id": 90171,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90171.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Well, Americans just pay too much for the prescription drugs that they need. And in fact, we pay way more in this country than people in other similar wealthy and large countries. And so one of the reasons that this happens is because the prescription drug companies in this country have so much market power. And I think that they actually game the system in some ways. And so what my bill does is it closes one of the loopholes that they use to keep lower cost generic drugs off the market. You know, a generic drug can be a very affordable alternative to a name brand drug and can sometimes cost 80% less money. But what these big drug companies do is they kind of gain the system to kind of keep these lower cost generics off the market, sometimes for years and years and years. And my bill closes that loophole. We're going to be voting on it in a committee hearing next week. And I'm very optimistic. It's a bipartisan bill that we'll be able to get this done.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
